From 8e8fa11ced022e364477a528e9a3f68e93932434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:48:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/imx: dw_mipi_dsi-imx: round pixel clock through the
 real LCDIF clock

Upstream-Status: Pending

dw_mipi_dsi_mode_fixup() was rewritten upstream to derive
adjusted_mode->clock purely from the DPHY's PLL math
(hs_clk_rate * lanes / bpp), never touching the actual LCDIF pixel
clock hardware at all. scarthgap's older version always rounded the
requested pixel clock through clk_round_rate(dsi->pixel_clk, ...)
before using it.

adjusted_mode->clock feeds drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(), which computes
every CRTC hsync/vsync/blanking timing count downstream. If that
value doesn't match the clock rate the hardware is actually driven
at, the CRTC timing generator and the real pixel clock drift out of
phase across each line -- producing a diagonal shearing artifact.
The DPHY's PLL and the LCDIF's pixel clock are two independent clock
domains (DPHY runs from mipi_phy_cfg_root/video_pll's DPHY-side PLL,
LCDIF's pixel clock is media_disp_pix off the shared video_pll), so
there is no reason the DPHY-derived value should match what the
LCDIF can actually achieve -- confirmed on real hardware that they
don't (49.5MHz actual vs. 50MHz nominal/DPHY-derived on this panel).

Second of three related fixes for DSI shearing on
imx93-cargt-00363-00365; see the accompanying clk-imx93.c and
device-tree patches for the other two. All three are needed
together -- confirmed on real hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c
index 0fca33f54f6a..cbe51d9a6739 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dw_mipi_dsi-imx.c
@@ -229,6 +229,18 @@ static bool dw_mipi_dsi_mode_fixup(void *priv_data,
 	}
 
 	pixel_clock_rate = phycfg.mipi_dphy.hs_clk_rate * dsi->lanes / bpp;
+	/*
+	 * Cargt: pixel_clock_rate above is derived purely from the DPHY's
+	 * PLL math, not from what the LCDIF pixel clock can actually
+	 * achieve. Round it through the real clock so adjusted_mode->clock
+	 * (used for all CRTC hsync/vsync/blanking timing math) matches the
+	 * clock rate the hardware is actually driven at -- a mismatch here
+	 * causes the CRTC timing generator and the real pixel clock to
+	 * drift out of phase across a line, producing a diagonal shearing
+	 * artifact. scarthgap's older mode_fixup always rounded through
+	 * clk_round_rate() for this reason; this rewrite dropped it.
+	 */
+	pixel_clock_rate = clk_round_rate(dsi->pixel_clk, pixel_clock_rate);
 	adjusted_mode->clock = pixel_clock_rate / MSEC_PER_SEC;
 
 	/* Workarounds for modes that need to round htotal up. */
